---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
---

<Layout>
	<div class="column-container">
		<div class="column">
			<section>
				<h2 class="subtitle">About Us</h2>
				<p>
					The Burlington Chess Club hosts weekly chess tournaments
					every Tuesday at 7 PM (with pairings posted by 7:30). The
					tournaments are CFC rated and span five rounds, with one
					round per week. The time control is 60 min + 30 sec bonus.
					We also host rapid and blitz tournaments throughout the
					year.
				</p>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h2 class="subtitle">Location</h2>
				<a
					target="_blank"
					href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/Wellington+Square+United+Church/@43.3311781,-79.7974956,120m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m6!3m5!1s0x882c9e2611e3b0ff:0xeedabac47797a553!8m2!3d43.3311045!4d-79.7970849!16s%2Fg%2F1tl4dp3t?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI1MDkwNy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D"
				>
					Wellington Square United Church 2121 Caroline Street,
					Burlington, Ontario, L7R 1L7
				</a>
				<p>
					Entrance is from the parking lot in the rear.
					<br />
					The playing area is in the gym in the middle of the building.
					<br />
					Casual play is in the Music Room across the foyer.
				</p>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h2 class="subtitle">Joining the Club</h2>
				<h3>Annual Membership</h3>
				<p>
					The annual membership covers all of the 5 round classical
					tournaments, as well as the rapid and blitz events held
					throughout the year.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>$150</strong> per year (e-transfer only)</li>
				</ul>
				<h3>Pay as You Play</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>$25</strong> for each 5-week CFC-rated tournament
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>$5</strong> for each additional junior from the same
						family
					</li>
					<li><strong>$5</strong> per night for casual play</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					<strong>E-transfer:</strong>{" "}
					<a href="mailto:burlingtonchess@gmail.com"
						>burlingtonchess@gmail.com</a
					>
				</p>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h2 class="subtitle">Casual Players Welcome</h2>
				<p>
					If you are newer to chess or not interested in playing
					competitively, our casual chess section will be perfect for
					you! Each night of casual chess costs only $5. Play against
					other newer players or challenge existing club members, all
					while expanding your chess knowledge.
					<br />
					If you are newer to chess or not interested in playing competitively,
					our casual chess section will be perfect for you! Each night of
					casual chess costs only $5. Play against other newer players or
					challenge existing club members, all while expanding your chess
					knowledge.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
		<div class="column">
			<section>
				<h2 class="subtitle">Tournaments</h2>
				<div class="tournaments-section">
					<div>
						<p>
							Our tournaments are scheduled for one game per week
							for five weeks. In order to play in these
							tournaments, a CFC membership is required:
						</p>
						<ul class="membership-list">
							<li>CFC Membership - Adult = $48/year</li>
							<li>CFC Membership - Junior = $32/year</li>
							<li>
								<a
									href="https://www.chess.ca/en/players/membership-fees/"
									>https://www.chess.ca<wbr />/en<wbr
									/>/players<wbr />/membership-fees/</a
								>
							</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p>
							You are required to obey the laws of chess and abide
							by proper chess etiquette:
						</p>
						<ol>
							<li>
								You must keep score of both your moves and your
								opponent’s moves
							</li>
							<li>
								If you touch a piece, you must move it (if it's
								legal)
							</li>
							<li>
								If you touch an opponent's piece, you must take
								it (if it's legal)
							</li>
							<li>
								You must castle with one hand, moving the king
								first
							</li>
							<li>
								You must make your move and press the clock with
								the same hand
							</li>
							<li>
								Your move is not complete until your clock has
								been pressed
							</li>
							<li>
								You must not talk, make noise, or disturb your
								opponent (or anyone else)
							</li>
						</ol>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p>
							Time control is 60 minutes per player with an
							increment of 30 seconds from the first move. (i.e.
							30 seconds is added to your clock after you complete
							each move).
						</p>
						<p>
							We ask that people show up by 7:15, so we can do the
							pairings and start at 7:30.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h2 class="subtitle">Casual Play</h2>
				<p>
					For those who are not ready to join the CFC and play rated
					tournaments, casual play is now available. With casual play,
					you need not keep score or use a clock.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
